Changes with nginx 1.29.5                                        15 Jun 2026

    *) Feature: HTTP response status codes are now managed through a
       centralized, registry-backed API.  The ngx_http_status_set()
       function is the single point that assigns a response status, and
       the ngx_http_status_reason(), ngx_http_status_validate(),
       ngx_http_status_register(), and ngx_http_status_is_cacheable()
       functions provide reason phrases, RFC 9110 metadata, a
       registration seam, and cacheability information.

    *) Feature: optional RFC 9110 status code validation can be enabled
       with the "--with-http_status_validation" configure option;
       validation is disabled by default and adds no overhead when it is
       not enabled.

    *) Change: the status reason-phrase lookup now routes through the new
       status registry via ngx_http_status_reason(), and the error-page
       lookup is now registry-fed -- gated by ngx_http_status_validate(),
       keyed by status code, and reading the registry class flags for the
       MSIE/Chrome body padding decision -- so the divergent
       NGX_HTTP_LAST_2XX and NGX_HTTP_OFF_* offset macros have been removed
       from both files.  The static error-page bodies are retained
       unchanged; status lines and error-page bodies remain byte-identical
       to previous releases, and the nginx-specific status codes 444 and
       494-499 are preserved.
